    "text": "> Sender sends segments | and 2, which are acknowledged immediately by an ACK. > Segment 3 1s lost. The receiver receives segment 4, which is out of order. > The receiver stores the data in the segment in its buffer but leaves a gap to indicate that there is no continuity in the data. > The receiver immediately sends an acknowledgment to the sender, displaying the next byte it expects. > Receiver stores bytes 801 to 900, but never delivers these bytes to the application until the gap is filled. > The receiver TCP delivers only ordered data to the process.",
